From: macOS-Pad-6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NativeUfs: kernel memory interfaces of xnu-12377, as UniXNU/ShengUfs 99d8bcd

SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause-Patent

xVanTuring/PipaUfs 5c64c01 (feeds.toml ShengUfs) still uses the vm_kern.h/vm_map.h interfaces of the iPadOS 17
kernel. Built against xnu-12377.121.6 (the macOS 26.5 profile, source storage recipe, kernel-build run
43105063854) it stops at kma_flags_t/KMA_KOBJECT/KMA_DATA (now in vm/vm_kern_xnu.h), kmem_free (same) and
vm_map_protect (gone; mach_vm_protect). This takes the same two changes the catalog's ShengUfs pin made:
include vm/vm_kern_xnu.h when it exists, and mach_vm_protect(map, addr, size, set_maximum = TRUE, VM_PROT_READ),
the call vm_map_protect(map, start, end, VM_PROT_READ, set_max = TRUE) made. Behaviour unchanged; the policy
storage stays read only after it is written. On pipa this path is not reached (no root policies).

diff --git a/NativeUfs.cpp b/NativeUfs.cpp
index 6301862..62364dd 100644
--- a/NativeUfs.cpp
+++ b/NativeUfs.cpp
@@ -7,6 +7,11 @@
 #include <libkern/crypto/sha2.h>
 #include <vm/vm_kern.h>
 #include <vm/vm_map.h>
+/* Newer XNU keeps the kernel memory and map protection interfaces in these headers. */
+#if __has_include(<vm/vm_kern_xnu.h>)
+#include <vm/vm_kern_xnu.h>
+#endif
+#include <mach/mach_vm.h>
 #include <sys/param.h>
 #if defined(NATIVE_VERIFIED_BLOCK) && NATIVE_VERIFIED_BLOCK
 #include "verified_root.h"
@@ -1898,8 +1903,8 @@ bool NativeUfsBlock::configureVerification ()
   uint8_t *key = reinterpret_cast<uint8_t *> (verifiedStorage + tableBytes);
   memcpy (key, verified_root_key, VR_KEY_BYTES);
   gRootDiagnostic.stage = "policy read-only protection";
-  if (vm_map_protect (kernel_map, verifiedStorage, verifiedStorage + verifiedStorageBytes,
-                      VM_PROT_READ, TRUE) != KERN_SUCCESS) {
+  if (mach_vm_protect (kernel_map, verifiedStorage, verifiedStorageBytes,
+                       TRUE, VM_PROT_READ) != KERN_SUCCESS) {
     return false;
   }
   gRootDiagnostic.stage = "owner signature and hash table";
